From: Josep Maria Viñolas Auquer <josepmaria@isardvdi.com>
Subject: [PATCH] RDP: report a FreeRDP failure through guac_rdp_client_abort()

With the busy-loop fix the connection loop also exits when FreeRDP has
recorded an error before freerdp_shall_disconnect() is set. That path
reported a generic "Connection closed." (UPSTREAM_UNAVAILABLE), so a user
logoff reached the client as an error and the web viewer reconnected.
Translate the FreeRDP error info instead, as the closing path does.
---
diff --git a/src/protocols/rdp/rdp.c b/src/protocols/rdp/rdp.c
--- a/src/protocols/rdp/rdp.c
+++ b/src/protocols/rdp/rdp.c
@@ -652,8 +652,10 @@
         /* Handle any input events that have been received */
         guac_rdp_handle_input_events(rdp_client);
 
-        /* Close connection cleanly if server is disconnecting */
-        if (connection_closing)
+        /* Close connection cleanly if server is disconnecting, or report why
+         * FreeRDP failed (a logoff must not look like a transport error) */
+        if (connection_closing || (wait_result < 0
+                    && freerdp_get_last_error(GUAC_RDP_CONTEXT(rdp_inst)) != FREERDP_ERROR_SUCCESS))
             guac_rdp_client_abort(client, rdp_inst);
 
         /* If a low-level connection error occurred, fail */
